  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently when grabbing or just before grabbing a VRCPickup object there is no convenient way to get the position (and rotation if that changes) of where the object will be attached to the player.\n\nEstimating the position can be tricky since the player's attachment point differs from their hand position, the objects tend to interpolate towards the player over time if grabbed from a distance and while moving the pickup around while held the object tends to lag behind the player's attachment point.\n\nExample API:\n\nVector3 VRCPickup.GetHeldPosition(VRCPlayerApi targetPlayer, PickupHand targetHand)\n\nReturns the world space position of where the pickup object will be attached to the specified player's hand.\n\nIf the object's rotation changes there could also be a VRCPickup.GetHeldRotation method that does a similar thing.",
